From 62e86865f1f1135d12c497a24108e8ad028c7092 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:47:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Polycrystal: displacement and stresses exported to ParaView
 in the same files

With the displacement (--enable-paraview-export) and the von Mises stress
(--enable-export-von-Mises-stress), the polycrystal wrote two ParaView
collections, OutputFile-Uniaxial-polycrystal and PolycrystalParaviewOutput,
each one writing the whole mesh at each step: for 600 grains on one node
and 20 steps, 6.1 and 4.4 GB, most of the second one being its mesh.

When both are exported, the stresses (von Mises stress, first eigen
stress) are now written with the displacement, in the same files, by the
export of the displacement of mfem-mgis (ParaviewExportResults::addField):
one collection, PolycrystalParaviewResults, with one mesh per step, whose
cycle k is the end of the step k + 1, as in the two other collections. The
L2 projections of the stresses are the same: they are computed by one
function, which gives them for a state of the materials, used by both
exports.

For 600 grains on one node, 20 steps: one collection of 7.5 GB (101 files)
against two of 6.5 and 4.7 GB (202 files); the files are written in 255 s
against about 354 s, and the computation takes 531 s against 603 s.

With one export only, nothing changes: the displacement alone is still
written in OutputFile-Uniaxial-polycrystal, the stresses alone in
PolycrystalParaviewOutput. The collection of the stresses is no longer
created when the stresses are exported with the displacement.

UniaxialPolycrystalTest-ParaviewExports (check-paraview-exports.py): the
displacement alone, the von Mises stress alone, and both in single
precision are written in the expected collection only, with the expected
fields, one mesh per file and the expected precision.
